WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.507
This query creates normalized email and name keys.

00:00:03.507 --> 00:00:06.662
It groups rows by those normalized values.

00:00:06.662 --> 00:00:10.522
Groups with more than one row become duplicate candidates.

00:00:10.522 --> 00:00:14.852
ARRAY_AGG shows the source IDs in each group.

00:00:14.852 --> 00:00:20.162
This is detection only. It does not yet say which source row is better.

00:00:20.162 --> 00:00:25.917
Standardization should make equivalent values comparable without inventing facts.

00:00:25.917 --> 00:00:33.972
Lowercasing an email or normalizing a known category map is different from guessing what an ambiguous value

00:00:33.972 --> 00:00:39.177
was supposed to mean. Good cleaning reduces representation noise while preserving uncertainty.
